# The stage0 compiler's back end: the program the checker collected, written as
# one C file. The file is a fixed prelude (the runtime: console output and the
# checked arithmetic, each trapping with exit code 70 as `refined run` does),
# then `main`:
#
# - every value becomes a typed C local named `v_<name>` (`const char *` for
#   `String`, `int64_t` for `Int64`, `int` for `ExitCode`, `bool` for `Bool`),
#   declared first with a zero value, then set in order: constants, then lets
#   (a let set from another value reads it, so constants come first);
# - every call that can fail gets a flag `f_<name>`, set by the call;
# - every loop header with a `maxIterations` bound gets a counter `n_<label>`;
# - every label becomes a C label `l_<label>` and its steps follow it: `do`
#   becomes a C statement or runtime call, `set` an assignment, `goto` and
#   `branch` C `goto`s, and `return ok` a C `return`.
#
# A jump to a bounded loop header counts the pass when it comes from inside
# the loop (from the header or a block within it) and resets the count when it
# enters the loop from outside, the rule the LLVM backend follows, so a loop
# that passes its bound traps in C as it does under `refined run`.
#
# C spellings are looked up by the target's and type's names in this module's
# own tables, so the checker and the emitter each keep only what they need.

emitc is module
emitc purpose "Write a checked stage0 program as one C file"
emitc path emitc
emitc imports standard.string
emitc imports standard.buffer
emitc imports standard.list
emitc imports standard.map
emitc imports standard.math
emitc imports standard.compare
emitc imports standard.logic
emitc imports standard.test
emitc imports lexer
emitc imports syntax
emitc imports model
emitc imports subset
emitc exports emitProgram

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- C spellings

CTarget is record
CTarget purpose "How a call target is written in C: the text before, between, and after its arguments"
CTarget typeParameter none
CTarget field text String
CTarget field before String
CTarget field between String
CTarget field after String

